docs/review-v04-claude-opus.txt:4:- **Effort is dead end-to-end.** `bindingsFromSheet` writes `effort` (`src/modelSheet.mjs:143`) but `resolveRoleBinding` returns only runtime/model/permissionProfile (`src/config.mjs:61-65`) and neither `buildClaudeArgv` nor `buildCodexArgv` emit a reasoning flag (`src/permissions.mjs:44-83`).
docs/review-v04-claude-opus.txt:5:- **Sequential, not fan-out.** `src/run.mjs:394-421` is a `for…of` loop; independent steps (reviewers a/b/c, runners a/b) run serially.
docs/review-v04-claude-opus.txt:6:- **Codex passes the full prompt as argv** (`src/runtimes/codex.mjs:42`, emitted in `worker.spawned.argv` at :51-60), while Claude uses stdin (`src/runtimes/claude.mjs:57`).
docs/review-v04-claude-opus.txt:11:**GO-with-fixes** — architecture is sound and the read-only boundary holds, but a validation-role mismatch and the sequential-vs-fanout gap should land before a production `/zedpstack`.
docs/review-v04-claude-opus.txt:22:| Medium | Gaps vs pstack | Independent steps run sequentially; pstack fans out reviewers/runners in parallel. 3 reviewers + lead run one-at-a-time (`src/run.mjs:394-421`). | Group steps with no shared `inputFrom` into a `Promise.all` wave; manifest already tracks per-step state. |
docs/review-v04-claude-opus.txt:23:| Medium | Correctness / security | Codex receives the entire rendered prompt (incl. `--context-file` diff) as an argv element and records it in `worker.spawned.argv`; large diffs risk `E2BIG`, and the prompt is visible via `ps` / persisted in `events.jsonl` (`src/runtimes/codex.mjs:42,51-60`). Claude avoids this via stdin. | Pass the prompt to Codex via stdin/file and redact/omit the prompt arg from the emitted `argv`. |
docs/review-v04-claude-opus.txt:25:| Low | Setup / sheet parse | When a sheet row lists more models than mapped zed roles (e.g. 3 values for `architect runners` → 2 roles), the extra value silently overwrites the last role (`src/modelSheet.mjs:136`). | Push overflow values into `droppedLines` or warn in the `setup apply` result. |
docs/review-v04-claude-opus.txt:30:- **Fix the reviewer validation role matching and wire `effort` through** (`resolveRoleBinding` → runtime argv, e.g. Codex `-c model_reasoning_effort`), or explicitly drop `effort` from the sheet/SKILL so config doesn't carry dead contract.
docs/review-v04-claude-opus.txt:31:- **Parallel fan-out for independent steps** to match "pstack completo" latency; sequential 3×-reviewer runs are the main parity/perf gap.
docs/review-v04-claude-opus.txt:32:- **Harden `watch`/Codex-argv ergonomics**: auto-exit watch on terminal run state and move Codex prompts off argv (stdin/file) to avoid `E2BIG` and prompt leakage in `events.jsonl`/`ps`.
